    "monograph": "<details>\n<summary>Does Fosfomycin cover CRAB?</summary>\n\n**Fosfomycin does not reliably cover CRAB (carbapenem-resistant Acinetobacter baumannii) as monotherapy.**\n\n- _A. baumannii_ is generally considered **intrinsically resistant to fosfomycin** due to its efflux mechanisms and genetic resistance determinants (e.g., abaF). Most CRAB clinical isolates have very high MICs to fosfomycin, far above achievable serum concentrations.[academic.oup+2](https://academic.oup.com/jac/article/72/1/68/2643136)\n\n**Key points from recent studies and stewardship reviews:**\n\n- **Combination therapy:** Intravenous fosfomycin has been used as part of combination regimens—with sulbactam, colistin, cefiderocol, or ampicillin/sulbactam—showing some benefit for severe CRAB infections.[pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih+5](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38697579/)\n    - _Example:_ Colistin plus fosfomycin or fosfomycin plus sulbactam shows bacterial killing and some clinical benefit, but clinical failures and resistance development are common if used alone.[pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih+2](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9686642/)\n- **Clinical outcomes:** Fosfomycin-containing regimens (not monotherapy) have been studied for ventilator-associated pneumonia, bacteremia, and catheter-related infections caused by CRAB, especially where few other options are available.[sciencedirect+4](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924857924002814)\n- **Mechanisms:** Disruption of certain efflux pumps in _A. baumannii_ can increase fosfomycin susceptibility, but clinical strains are usually strongly resistant and rapidly develop further resistance during exposure.[academic.oup](https://academic.oup.com/jac/article/72/1/68/2643136)\n\n**Summary:**\n\n- **Fosfomycin-alone NOT recommended for CRAB.**\n- **May be considered ONLY as part of multidrug regimens,** preferably guided by microbiology susceptibility and infectious disease consultation.[pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih+3](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9961360/)\n- Monitor for rapid development of resistance when used with _A. baumannii_; always combine with other active agents (e.g., sulbactam, polymyxin, cefiderocol, colistin).\n\n**References:**[sciencedirect+9](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924857924001080)\n\n\nIf you need details on specific synergistic combinations, clinical protocols, or susceptibility breakpoints, let me know!\n\n1. [https://academic.oup.com/jac/article/72/1/68/2643136](https://academic.oup.com/jac/article/72/1/68/2643136)\n2. [https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/2018/3893492](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/2018/3893492)\n3. [https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5822792/](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5822792/)\n4. [https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38697579/](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38697579/)\n5. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924857924002814](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924857924002814)\n6. [https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9686642/](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9686642/)\n7. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924857924001080](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924857924001080)\n8. [https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/cellular-and-infection-microbiology/articles/10.3389/fcimb.2024.1395260/full](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/cellular-and-infection-microbiology/articles/10.3389/fcimb.2024.1395260/full)\n9. [https://journals.asm.org/doi/10.1128/aac.02435-13?doi=10.1128%2Faac.02435-13](https://journals.asm.org/doi/10.1128/aac.02435-13?doi=10.1128%2Faac.02435-13)\n10. [https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9961360/](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9961360/)\n11. [https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-021-04303-7](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-021-04303-7)\n12. [https://www.journalmeddbu.com/tur/tam-metin/288](https://www.journalmeddbu.com/tur/tam-metin/288)\n13. [https://ascpt.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/cts.70038](https://ascpt.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/cts.70038)\n14. [https://pesquisa.bvsalud.org/portal/resource/pt/wpr-890919](https://pesquisa.bvsalud.org/portal/resource/pt/wpr-890919)\n15. [https://www.clinicalkey.jp](https://www.clinicalkey.jp/)\n16. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1567134821002409](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1567134821002409)\n\n</details>",
